<header class="entry-header">
<h1 class="entry-title">Nha Rong Wharf</h1>
</header>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="page-spacer clearfix">
<div class="content-area" id="primary">
<div class="container">
<div class="row">
<main class="site-main col-xs-12 col-sm-8 left-block" id="main">
<article class="post hentry">
<a href="/en/blog-details.html">
</a>
<header class="entry-header">
</header>
<div class="entry-content">
<div class="post-frame">
<img alt="Post image" src="/images/use_img/bthcm1.jpeg"/>
<div class="img-ref">Source: vinwonders.com</div>
</div>
<h3>Introductory Article:</h3>
<h4>• Introduction:</h4>
<p>
  You visit Ho Chi Minh City and want to have a peaceful and windy place where you can relax and admire the skyscrapers, high-rise buildings and the bustling bustle of the city. In the city, you should choose the historical site of Nha Rong Wharf - the oldest trading port of Vietnam. Not only is that, for Vietnamese people, Nha Rong Wharf one of the places of special historical significance. This port is where Uncle Ho went to find a way to save the country and change history for the nation. Currently, Nha Rong Wharf is a place to store and display many artifacts and images of people and Vietnam's history. Therefore, you can also visit and learn about the life and history of the nation, especially President Ho Chi Minh's journey to find a way to save the country.
</p>
<div class="post-frame">
<img alt="Post image" src="/images/use_img/bthcm2.jpeg"/>
<div class="img-ref">Source: vinwonders.com</div>
</div>
<h4>• History:</h4>
<p>
•	Previously, this place used to be the headquarters of the Saigon trading port, built by the French colonialists in 1863. Although it is a work built by the French in Western style, the roof is designed according to Vietnamese culture. The South with the dragon is adoring the moon, so the locals are usually "Nha Rong" and the nearby harbor is "Nha Rong Wharf". <br/>
•	At this port, on June 5, 1911, Uncle Ho boarded the ship Admiral Latouche Tréville to leave Vietnam for France and begin the journey to make great victories for the nation.<br/>
•	Because of this extremely important historical significance, when Vietnam achieved independence and reunification in 1975, this place became a memorial to Ho Chi Minh. In 1995, this relic was repaired and changed to Ho Chi Minh Museum, becoming a symbol of the city.
</p>
<div class="post-frame">
<img alt="Post image" src="/images/use_img/bthcm3.webp"/>
<div class="img-ref">Source: tourpro.vn</div>
</div>
<h4>• Values</h4>
<p>
 1.	Unique architecture: Nha Rong Wharf is the oldest French architecture preserved in Saigon. Up to now, this relic after many times of middle school still retains its majestic majesty. Because the building was built by the French, the architecture here has bold Western impressions, luxurious. The building stands out with its reinforced concrete structure, which is relatively strong and can bear good forces. High concrete columns and reclining pillars help the building to withstand flood water, stormy winds and heavy traffic. The main color of the building is white, creating elegance and sophistication. The decorative patterns on the walls and windows are often classical French culture with delicate curving lines and attractive textures. Besides classical French architecture, Asian architectural features are also cleverly combined, creating a unique beauty, blending between Asia and Europe. In particular, on the top of the roof of the building, there are two dragons facing each other with the meaning "Two dragons adoring the moon". Although this is a common image in Asian culture, the difference is that the middle of the two dragon heads is not carved with a moon face, but a badge with the shape of a horse's head and an anchor. In 1955, the government of the Republic of Vietnam renovated the building and replaced the two old dragons with two new dragons with the head facing out.<br/>
2.	With a prime location overlooking the Saigon River, the harbor owns an extremely spacious and airy campus. When walking around here, you will feel the cool breeze from the river blowing in, letting your soul enjoy the view of the city. The two best relaxing times for you to enjoy the scenery here are sunset and evening, you will see the whole area shimmering and fanciful, worthy of the name "Pearl of the Far East".<br/>
3.	Ho Chi Minh Museum: The main part of the building is now the Ho Chi Minh Museum, Ho Chi Minh City branch. The museum has an area of 1500 m² with 9 exhibition booths, circulating a lot of precious and precious materials. Specifically, the museum is currently storing and displaying about 11,372 documents and artifacts along with about 3,300 books with topics on President Ho Chi Minh. Artifacts are displayed in many different spaces to create excitement for visitors. This place helps people better understand the life and revolutionary career of the genius leader of the country, the beloved old father of the nation.
</p>
</div>
</article>
